!}

= The Red Army Marches West

In April Piłsudski's Poland invaded the Ukraine and took Kiev. The Red Army has thrown it back, and in July Tukhachevsky's armies take Minsk and Vilna and cross into Poland proper. In a few weeks they may stand on the border of East Prussia.

The German government declares its neutrality. French munitions for Poland still cross Germany by rail. The Danzig dockers have refused to unload them, and railwaymen in Saxony and the Rhineland are stopping trains on their own account. [? if e20_polish_dir = 1 : A telegram from Lenin has reached the Zentrale: not one train for Piłsudski. ?]

- @unions: Block the munitions with the unions and the USPD.
- @prepare: Prepare to rise when the Red Army reaches the border.
- @bayonets: Stop the trains, and say the German revolution will not come on Russian bayonets.

@unions
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A legal blockade, with the transport workers' union behind it.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids a common front with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.warsaw_bonus += 1;
Q.uspd_score += 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
RG.comply(30);
!}

The transport workers' union bans war material for Poland. The USPD holds meetings in every city.

@prepare
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The districts in the east will be ready if the Red Army comes. So will the police.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids preparing an armed rising.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.warsaw_bonus += 1;
Q.border_rising = 1;
Q.repression += 8;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
RG.comply(45);
RG.ecci('bukharin', 6);
!}

In East Prussia and Silesia our members dig up the rifles of March and draw up lists of bridges and police barracks.

@bayonets
subtitle: Radek will call it pacifism.
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence += 5;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
RG.comply(15);
RG.ecci('radek', -6);
!}

Our railwaymen stop two trains at Halle. *Die Rote Fahne* calls for peace with Soviet Russia and adds that the German workers will make their own revolution.
